Z||000000||beachbomb||07-13-2001||01:56 PM||||Hey all, driving home from work today on I-95, i gun it a little to pass a truck and the engine dies and then a real strong smell of gas!, i pull over and try to start it but acts like its not getting fuel..i also tried to hear if the fuel pump would come on when i turn the key to run,(pump was usually a little loud anyway but i never thought anything of it) i don't think i could hear it(there was alot of traffic noise so it was kinda hard to hear). Are these all symptoms of a blown fuel pump, plmk what you think...thanks Jim<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_19.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-13-2001||02:10 PM||||If you smell gas, youm ust be getting fuel. I would suspect the ignition module. Check for spark.||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||07-13-2001||03:06 PM||||Hey wolfhound, acutally the only time i had the smell of gas is when it initally died on me, i had thought of the ignition module at first but never got the smell of gas after that moment...thanks..jim||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||07-13-2001||03:17 PM||||OK, It,s an Indy 2.5, Pull the air filter cover off and have someone try to start the car. look to see if it,s getting gas.<P>I always try to check the easy fixes first.<BR>It sometimes pays off , sometimes not.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||07-13-2001||05:07 PM||||Hope it's not the cam gear, Jim.. that is what happened to my 88 coupe....<P>Good luck...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||starfighter007@msn.com||07-13-2001||05:56 PM||||My vote is for the fuel pumpbut wait something like this happened to me last year almost exactly what you describe passing the truck whole bit. but after a the car would sit for a little while the pump would cool off and it would start again I kept doing this till I could make of the inter state to a repair shop and it was the fuel pump.hmmmm anyway still do the easy check and see if the pum is working||||reg||1
Z||000006||beachbomb||07-13-2001||06:57 PM||||Hey all, thanks for you're advice, i had the car towed to a repair shop..why not fix it myself, well.. 1)i was in my Complete White Navy uniform in a 97 degree day on an interstate, needless to say i couldn't troubleshoot to much on my own without ruining my uniform, 2)i just pulled an engine and transmission out of my spare Indy last weekend and i'm pretty well tired of working on cars for a while!!<BR>It did aggreivate me that i really couldn't troubleshoot it on my own because of the White uniform thing, i hate taking cars to the repair shop!!!!, i'll let you all know what the actual problem was on Monday..Jim(fiero-less this week-end!!!!) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
